  "id": "total-variance",
  "term": "total variance",
  "definition": "Total variance is the overall amount of variability in the outcome being studied. In effect-size reporting, it is the full variation used as the reference point, so a value such as eta squared can express how much of that overall variability is explained by group membership or another effect.",
